.TH EXPOSE 1
.SH NAME
expose \\- report local listener exposure evidence
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B expose
expose [--format json]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reports local listener evidence and identifies firewall and external-reachability information it cannot observe.
.SH OPTIONS
Use \fBexpose --help\fR for the complete, version-specific flag list.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Uses the shared CLI status convention: 0 success, 1 a completed negative finding or policy failure, 2 invalid usage, 3 a partial result, and 4 a runtime failure. Not every status applies to every command.
